1. THE ENVELOPE THE GRADES ARE JUDGED AGAINST (pcb_envelope.yaml, read back)
   in use -20 to 40 C ambient; the worst inside air, lid closed, 62.1 C (the board air a part is judged against until T-H1); storage 3 months -20 to 45 C;
   the owner's qualification margins (D-02a): operate at +55 C, store at +71 C and -33 C, survive and recover. Verdicts: INSIDE when the maker's
   operating row strictly covers -20 to 62.1 C; AT_LIMIT when it meets an end exactly; OUTSIDE otherwise; NOT READ when no row is read at the source.

